## Pre-work plan

- Background: official Renderer/Interactive.Client 0.2.5 pass owner tests and package provenance, but Daedalus formal 18884 reports 16 failures when a delayed previous authoritative response arrives during a navigator gesture.
- Goal: reproduce the exact delayed-response ordering in an owner test, fix the earliest owner authority gap, and publish a new exact package graph only after owner RED->GREEN proof.
- Assumptions: Daedalus evidence is read-only; Research host 18884 and consumer source remain Daedalus-owned; existing navigator actions and non-delayed paths must remain unchanged.
- Steps: project bounded evidence; verify package WebSharper asset provenance; compare source and consumer fixture ordering; add failing owner regression; apply the smallest Renderer/Client correction; run focused Expecto and owner Playwright; package, verify, document, commit/push, then hand back exact authority.
- Scope: owner Renderer/Interactive.Client, owner tests/BrowserDemo, RFC-0036 current traceability, and release evidence. No Research host lifecycle changes.
- Acceptance: active gesture geometry is stable across delayed previous and newer authoritative frames, pointerup emits exactly one intent, matching response settles once after the terminal event, existing 68 focused tests and Playwright parity remain green, and official package assets/DLLs match committed source.
- Risk: conflating DLL provenance with WebSharper asset provenance, or weakening authoritative settlement after pointerup. Both are explicit gates.

